1
00:00:02,158 --> 00:00:04,450
INSTRUCTOR: Hello, everyone,
and welcome to the content

2
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:07,618
video for how to
update a Github repo.

3
00:00:07,618 --> 00:00:09,160
So this is something
that you'll have

4
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:11,717
to do multiple times
throughout the semester.

5
00:00:11,717 --> 00:00:14,050
Whenever I add anything or
change anything on the Github

6
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:16,420
repo, you'll need
to pull it down

7
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:19,700
to your repository
on your Cloud9 server

8
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:23,193
so you have all the up-to-date
code throughout the semester.

9
00:00:23,193 --> 00:00:24,110
So how do you do that?

10
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:25,068
Here's how you do that.

11
00:00:25,068 --> 00:00:26,770
So let's go into
the terminal here.

12
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:31,660
I'm going to type the command
clear to clear up my console.

13
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:35,500
OK, and now that I'm in here,
I'm going to do a git status,

14
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,243
which is going to tell
me I'm on the main branch

15
00:00:38,243 --> 00:00:39,410
and everything's up to date.

16
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:41,170
So here's what
you'll want to do.

17
00:00:41,170 --> 00:00:43,250
Let's say I put out
a message on Slack.

18
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:44,540
The repo has been updated.

19
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:47,140
There's code we're going
to cover this week.

20
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:48,320
Please update your repo.

21
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:49,528
Here's how you would do that.

22
00:00:49,528 --> 00:00:51,160
The command is
git pull, and that

23
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:53,710
will pull down all of the
code from the repo back

24
00:00:53,710 --> 00:00:55,940
into your local version.

25
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:57,345
Now mine says
already up to date,

26
00:00:57,345 --> 00:00:58,720
and that's the
message you'll get

27
00:00:58,720 --> 00:00:59,970
when everything is good to go.

28
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:03,020
When you're up to date
with the remote repo,

29
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:06,200
it'll say already up to
date with your local repo.

30
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:09,650
OK, but oftentimes if you've
changed things, which is great--

31
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:11,990
if you've changed things
in your local repo,

32
00:01:11,990 --> 00:01:13,630
it'll give you a message, hey--

33
00:01:13,630 --> 00:01:16,270
I forget the exact verbiage,
but basically, you've

34
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:19,430
updated things
locally or, you know,

35
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:21,620
there's edits that are
not being tracked locally.

36
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:23,000
So here's how you handle those.

37
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,760
You could merge them,
but you're never

38
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:26,240
going to push
anything to my repo,

39
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:28,660
so you really don't need to
worry about merging anything

40
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:31,150
because you're just going to
be a consumer of this repo

41
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:32,180
over and over.

42
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:36,040
So the command that you want to
just store your changes locally

43
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:39,490
that you made but still get the
new stuff from the repo, first

44
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:40,610
do a git stash.

45
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:42,760
So it'll be git stash
just like that git--

46
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,080
-G-I-T-- stash--

47
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,100
S-T-A-S-H. Hit Enter.

48
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,160
I'm not going to because
I want my changes to be

49
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:50,200
in sync with the remote repo.

50
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,017
Hit Enter.

51
00:01:51,017 --> 00:01:52,600
Then it'll say a
message like, keeping

52
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:56,450
track of these local
changes separately.

53
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:58,850
Then after you do a stash
and a git pull again,

54
00:01:58,850 --> 00:02:01,480
you should get the message
already up to date.

55
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:05,290
OK, so that's it, that
is how to keep in sync

56
00:02:05,290 --> 00:02:09,110
or keep repulling the code,
latest code from the repo.

57
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:10,639
That's the end of
the content video.

58
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:12,420
Thanks for watching.